FreeEOS 3.0.0 release notes

FreeEOS is a software library for calculating (by an extremely rapid
free-energy minimization method) an equation of state for physical
conditions in stellar interiors.  It uses a semi-empirical free-energy
model that has been adjusted to fit results from the more detailed
SCVH (Saumon, D., Chabrier, G., \& Van Horn, H. M. 1995ApJ...99.713)
and OPAL (Rogers, F. J., \& Nayfonov, A.  2002ApJ...576.1064R) EOS
calculations.  This is the latest release of this software and the
only version I support.

Note that most FreeEOS "bugs" are due to users not understanding the
doxygen argument documentation of the two different (legacy and
modern) versions of the free_eos generic Fortran subroutine that is
called by user's programmes. (Browse either
free_eos-3.0.0/document_FreeEOS/doxygen/doxygen/latex/FreeEOS_developer_documentation.pdf
or free_eos-3.0.0/document_FreeEOS/doxygen/doxygen/html/index.xhtml
for access to all doxygen-generated documentation of FreeEOS.)
Therefore to reduce wasting time with bug triage (as opposed to
spending time on actual development), I request if you encounter a
problem with this release such as not understanding that
documentation, use [the FreeEOS bug
tracker](https://sourceforge.net/p/freeeos/bugs/) to report the
problem *only if* the issue cannot be easily resolved by discussion on
[the freeeos-general mailing
list](https://sourceforge.net/projects/freeeos/lists/freeeos-general).

This software is distributed under the GPL version 2.0 or later.  See
the COPYING file for all licensing details.

